tual paper.\n\nNow I'm pulling together the D-study item requirements across all benchmarks—MMLU needs 510 items, ARC needs 340, HellaSwag needs 280, and GSM8K requires 1150 for adequate generalizability. The confidence intervals from the cross-model analysis show MMLU ranging from 430 to 610 items, while GSM8K's interval is quite wide at 600 to 2100, which limits how actionable that guidance is.\n\nI'm ready to draft the paper using these empirical estimates and will structure the citations with a numbered system, starting with foundational G-theory work from Shavelson and Webb, then moving through contemporary applications to LLM evaluation and hardware variance considerations. I've compiled the full reference list with 25 sources covering everything from item response theory to floating-point reproducibility issues. Now I'm ready to start writing the actual paper, though I need to finalize the title first to capture the core narrative about evaluation reproducibility and variability in language model benchmarking. I'm refining the title to drop \"Evaluation Metrics\" since the logprob analysis is limited, settling on \"Reproducibility Budgets for LLM Evaluation: Benchmark-Specific Variance Structures via Generalizability Theory\" — this captures the core concepts of reproducibility budgets, benchmark-specificity, and G-theory without overcommitting to metrics analysis. Now I'm ready to write.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17698,"cache_read_input_tokens":23439,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17698},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02938283-148b-4d87-8e7a-0555aca65786","uuid":"76ec6d6d-3809-44d7-ba25-5f4ad46b94e2"}
